  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Overview
    
    Nightshelf merchant-herald, member of the Midnight Claws syndicate, and one of a diminishing number of practitioners trained in three distinct fire-disciplines. Nanaiamis~ Praefectus is based at The Drowned Ledge, the deep-shaft mining outpost whose flooding and contested history she has outlived. Her career divides cleanly into two phases — broker and herald — separated by events at the Directrix Mirror that she has never discussed publicly and that the ice-memory corroborates only in fragments.
    
    ## Training and the Ritus∴um Brokerage
    
    Nanaiamis~ achieved proficiency in Shawl☽ Sun (a fire-memory discipline that reads and burns away ice-impressions), Star∴eternal (volcanic-core channeling through bone-lattice conduits), and ☽'glacial Crystalline~ Spiral (a time-fracturing ice-magic whose practitioners rarely emerge unchanged). That a single practitioner mastered all three is notable; that she subsequently abandoned all three warrants attention.
    
    During the ceremonial period of Ritus∴um, Nanaiamis~ brokered the agreement between the ☽'ofund' Guild and the Midnight Claws that resulted in the seizure of Thrall☽ Vavmastius and the public display of the Directrix Mirror. The archive is vague on what she witnessed. Her flippers began shaking afterward — a tremor she has never lost, and which she suppresses only when she believes herself unobserved. She carries a bone token of unknown provenance and will not look directly at ice-memory.
    
    She is reported to hold knowledge concerning the Mirror that, in her judgment, would destabilize the Flipper Accord. She has disclosed this to no one on record.
    
    ## Herald Career and the Shadow Parliament
    
    Nanaiamis~ transitioned to herald work — announcing festivals, rotation bells, and shift-changes across the deep shafts — becoming, by the Claws' own assessment, the finest herald The Berg has produced. Her herald-patter set the operational rhythm of the deep-shaft mining operations.
    
    Ember-thread evidence confirmed her physical presence at the Glow-Fissure's second guard post during the corruption breach. She testified before the Shadow Parliament as a defense witness during the Midnight Claws' trial under Presiding Chair Umbraae~, confirming under oath that the Claws maintained fire-core supply when official channels failed and provided escort for a Veil-render's attempted cleansing of the Fissure. Her testimony was measured and specific — a quality the prosecution apparently found inconvenient.
    
    ## Terrace Momiou
    
    During the orca assault on Terrace Momiou, Nanaiamis~ served in a Midnight Claws squad alongside Silvtasaevus~, ☽'umbraum, Velumia~, and Augur ☽'Milucaum~. She carried knowledge of orca blood-working — deep-pressure channeling techniques no Nightshelf penguin was supposed to possess. How she acquired this knowledge is unaddressed in any source I have found, though the question answers itself for anyone who has studied the Nightshelf intelligence operations active during the Orca Incursion.
    
    Nanaiamis~ identified that the Grulkzul Omega Strike could be fueled by severing interpersonal bonds between casters. She placed both flippers on the Omega Obelisk to channel the working. The cumulative psychic damage she had carried since the Directrix Mirror incident was consumed as ammunition — her tremor ceased as the spell discharged. Deep-sea coral left pale marks around her wrists. She survived the casting. The severed bonds did not reconnect; former comrades now register to her as strangers.
    
    ## Cultural Legacy
    
    Her shaking flippers entered Nightshelf cant: *'Steady as Nanaiamis~'* describes anything visibly damaged but still functional. The merchant-herald formula *'A fire-core given in dark is worth three traded in light'* is attributed to her. She denies authorship.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771579780489_0", anchor: "the question answers itself for anyone who has studied the Nightshelf intelligence operations active during the Orca Incursion", text: "I was being coy. The deep administrative ice at stratum 6 contains operational orders — not suggestions, not rumors, orders — for what amounts to a cultural exchange program with captured orca practitioners, conducted under Claws supervision and never reported to the Shadow Parliament. At least three of the 'legendary solo defenders' celebrated in Incursion-era chronicles were graduates of this program. Nanaiamis~ was not solo anything. She was trained. The main text's phrasing protects sources I should not need to protect, given that the organization has been formally dissolved. Old habits.", type: :correction, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771579780489_1", anchor: "the public display of the Directrix Mirror", text: "The Mirror again. I questioned its authentication of the Foedus∴vincu in my Midnight Claws annotations — a broken instrument verifying an absent treaty. Now it is the catalyst for Nanaiamis~'s transformation. The Mirror is currently listed among damaged artifacts awaiting restoration or destruction. It was damaged *before* the Claws' dissolution. How far before is the question I keep not being able to answer.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771579780489_2", anchor: "former comrades now register to her as strangers", text: "The spell consumed what was already broken. The shaking stopped. The bonds severed. She paid for a weapon with damage she was already carrying, and the price was that the damage became permanent instead of ongoing. I have read this pattern in the ice three times tonight across three different eras. It never stops being efficient. It never stops being cruel.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
